        <section>
          <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9"/>
          <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Assessment and Plan"/>
          <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>Patient reports severe muscle pain and weakness for past 2 weeks, particularly in thighs and shoulders. Difficulty climbing stairs and raising arms. Started atorvastatin 80mg 3 weeks ago post-MI. Multiple drug interactions with atorvastatin: 1) Diltiazem (added for rate control) increases atorvastatin levels via CYP3A4 inhibition, 2) Sertraline may increase myopathy risk, 3) CKD reduces statin clearance. Physical exam shows proximal muscle tenderness and weakness (4/5 strength). Ordered CK level (likely rhabdomyolysis). May need to reduce statin dose or switch to different statin.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
